  "body": "Stacked on #4364 (#4212). This PR depends on #4364: it reads the source face record that #4364 adds. This PR is opened against `main`, so its diff also shows the commits of that PR until it merges.\n\n## Build status\n\n- The commits of this PR were built and tested on the earlier base `773736856`. \"Tests\" below gives those runs.\n- Then they were rebased onto `main` `a721fd4dc` and the stacked PR, with no local build. The rebase had no conflicts. The code diff did not change: the patch-ids are the same.\n- This head was not built or tested locally. The maintainer's runners test it.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds two optional parts to MCP answers. No existing key changes. A model that has no SolidCraft names gives the same answers as before.\n\n### 1. SolidCraft face names\n\nWhen a model has the source face record of a `.sc` import (#4212), these rows get new keys:\n\n- each face row and each patch row of `list_features`;\n- each face pick and each patch pick that `picks_view` shows. This one hook serves `get_operation_geometry`, `set_operation_geometry`, `get_selection`, the area and \"Do not touch\" views, and `pick_in_box`.\n\nThe keys:\n\n- `source_name`: the SolidCraft name, when the face has one name.\n- `source_names`: the names, sorted, when the face or the patch has more than one name.\n- `source_unverified: true`: SolidCraft did not verify one of the names.\n\nA row gets no new key in these cases:\n\n- the model has no record;\n- the record does not tile the facets of the model;\n- the pick is not in the model now;\n- the name is blank.\n\nThe code never shows a wrong name set or a partial name set. Chains get no names (#4215).\n\n### 2. `changes` in the `import_model` answer for an update\n\nWhen `import_model` updates a model that was in the document before the call, the answer gets this key:\n\n```text\n\"changes\": {\n  \"faces\":   { \"carried\": N, \"added\": N, \"missing\": N },\n  \"patches\": { \"carried\": N, \"added\": N, \"missing\": N },\n  \"chains\":  { \"carried\": N, \"added\": N, \"missing\": N },\n  \"summary\": \"the phrase that the window shows after a re-import\"\n}\n```\n\n- The counts come from `revision::changes`. The window gets the same diff from `UpdateModel::changes`.\n- `summary` is `FeatureChanges::describe`.\n- A first import gets no `changes`. A refused import gets no `changes`.\n- This is the change summary that #3814 asks for. It is one of the five scope items of #3814.\n\n### Where the code is\n\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/source_names.rs` (new, 264 lines): the name set of a face id or of a patch. It is pure code and has 7 unit tests.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/source_names.rs` (new, 157 lines): it finds the record, builds the features and writes the keys.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/reimport_changes.rs` (new, 81 lines): it keeps the models before the import and adds `changes` after the import.\n- The hooks: 4 lines in `mcp/tools.rs::import_model`, 3 lines in `mcp/features.rs::list_features`, 2 lines in `mcp/pick.rs::picks_view`, and the `mod` lines.\n- `mcp/tools.rs` (444 lines on `main`, 448 after this PR) and `mcp/features.rs` (435 lines, 438 after) had more than 400 lines before this PR. This PR adds only the hook lines to them. The logic is in the new files.\n- `script/api.rs` does not change. #4212 and #4213 change `v_import`, so this PR does not touch that function. Thus a `cam.import` script does not get `changes`.\n- The name code builds the features from the model's own facets (`features_of_facets`). The feature caches use the content as the key, not the facet order. A cached `Features` can have a different facet order, and then each facet index points to a different facet.\n- No tool description changes. `mcp_doc_drift` passed on the earlier base.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/4214-mcp-face-names.md`.\n\n### Commits\n\nThe first 5 commits are the commits of #4364. They go out of this diff when it merges. The commits of this PR:\n\n1. `feat(mcp): import_model answers an update with its feature changes`\n2. `feat(mcp): show SolidCraft face names on features and picks`\n3. `test(mcp): a face pick on the .sc fixture shows its name`\n4. `test(mcp): fix the .sc pick test's pocket heights`\n5. `fix(mcp): name the snapshot type of reimport_changes::Before`\n6. `docs(decisions): file the PR's decisions under #4214`\n\nCommits 4 and 5 are the fixes that the build on the earlier base found: a test setup and a clippy `type_complexity` error.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew in `crates/geometry/src/geometry/source_names.rs`:\n\n- `each_box_side_reads_its_own_name`\n- `a_face_over_two_record_faces_has_both_names_sorted`\n- `an_unverified_name_is_flagged`\n- `a_record_that_does_not_fit_gives_no_names`\n- `an_id_that_is_not_in_the_mesh_has_no_name`\n- `a_blank_name_gives_no_name`\n- `a_patch_reads_the_names_of_all_its_strips`\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/mcp/source_names.rs`:\n\n- `each_face_row_names_its_solidcraft_face`\n- `a_face_over_two_record_faces_lists_both_and_flags_an_unverified_one`\n- `no_record_or_a_record_that_does_not_fit_shows_no_names`\n- `a_face_pick_shows_its_name_in_the_operation_geometry`\n- `a_patch_pick_names_all_its_faces_and_a_missing_pick_names_none`\n- `a_sc_import_names_every_face_and_patch`\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/mcp/reimport_changes.rs`:\n\n- `a_first_import_answers_with_no_changes`\n- `an_update_counts_what_moved_in_each_domain`\n- `the_same_file_again_carries_every_id`\n- `a_refused_update_answers_with_no_changes`\n\n`a_sc_import_names_every_face_and_patch` imports `testdata/models/hole_on_pocket_wall.sc` through the real import. Each face row and each patch row has a name. A face pick in `get_operation_geometry` shows the same keys as its `list_features` row.\n\nResults on the earlier base `773736856`, with the stacked PR's commits of that time:\n\n- All 17 tests of this PR: pass.\n- The app lib and the 167 app test binaries that `quick` maps to this diff: pass (1,372 tests, 0 failures).\n- All 39 geometry test binaries: pass (440 tests).\n- The clippy step of the batch tier (`-D warnings`, all gate crates) and the kernel: pass.\n- `mcp_doc_drift` and `mcp_pick`: pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **This head.** It was not built or tested locally (see \"Build status\").\n- **The full batch tier.** The diff touches `crates/geometry/`, so `quick` becomes `batch`. Batch needs more disk than the build machine has. The runs above are the replacement.\n- The light lane.\n- `cargo fmt --check`. On the build machine it fails for `camcraft-app` with \"os error 206\": the command line is too long. The repository has no `rustfmt.toml`. The new files use 120 columns, as the code around them.\n- The wasm build.\n- The cost of the names on a large `.sc` model. The names build the features from the facets for each call, with no cache. A model without a record does no extra work.\n- Linux and macOS.\n\n## Open points for the maintainer\n\n- **Fit with #3814.** The triage note on #4214 asks for your answer. This PR gives the counts that #3814 asks for, and `summary` in addition. It does not do the other four scope items of #3814. If you want #3814 separate, the commits for `changes` (1 and 5) can go as a PR of their own, with no dependency on #4364.\n- **The followed and lost picks** of the \"Done means\" of #4214 come from the PR of #4213: the `picks` key of the `import_model` answer. This PR and that PR together meet #4214.\n- **The counts do not match the `list_features` totals in two domains.** `changes.faces` counts each face id; `faces_total` counts planar faces only. `changes.chains` counts tangent chains; `chains_total` counts the chains of the pick graph.\n- **Unverified names are shown**, with `source_unverified: true`. The PR of #4213 does not follow them.\n- **No tool description changes.** One sentence for `changes` and one for `source_name` can come in a later PR, with the regenerated `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`.\n\nChangelog: MCP: `list_features` and the pick views give the SolidCraft name of each face and patch of a `.sc` model (`source_name`, `source_names`), and `import_model` gives the carried, added and missing feature counts of an update (`changes`).\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4214\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
